      "content": "yeah, that makes sense. i'm already starting to divert some stuff to a smaller online bank. but i'm worried that if they see a massive amount of money leaving all at once, they'll flag it as \"suspicious activity\" or something just to freeze the account and trap the rest of my savings. it's like they're waiting for me to make a move so they can pull the trigger. is there a way to drain my main account incrementally or use certain transfer types that won't trigger their internal security alarms while i'm trying to escape their control?",
